title A look takes the mail that arrived
sub Drawn from the intent before modeling: mail that arrives between looks is taken by one look, shown once, and given back when the look fails or ky restarts mid-look

== graph A look takes the mail that arrived
view: states
tone idle: Waiting
tone work: Working
[*] -> idle
group one: One look
idle: Waiting for its time {idle}
asking: Asking the model, with the mail it took {work}
posting: Posting what it found {work}
group end
group done: All mail
once: Every mail that arrived was shown once
  state: AllShownOnce
group end
!twice: The same mail is shown twice
  fails: ShownOnce
!stranded: A mail no look will ever show
  fails: NoneStranded
idle -> asking: its time comes
asking -> posting: the model answers
posting -> idle: it posts
asking -> idle: the model fails, or ky restarts
look: idle > asking > posting > idle => once | a look | At its time the look takes the waiting mail, asks, and posts it.
retry: idle > asking > idle > asking > posting > idle => once | fails, then the next look | The model fails; the mail goes back, and the next look shows it once.
